  "notes": "Official cause code is TBD/provisional on FORM-366 despite a detailed narrative root cause; cause node marked provisional per rule 4. Title in FORM-366 fields was truncated ('Full Reactor Scram due to an'); completed using narrative content. No SSCs were inoperable at event start and no component failed per se (LVDT wiring errors are described as a manufacturing defect discovered via the event, modeled as the origin FailureMode). RPS (JC) is the actuated system per reporting criterion; OPRM and EHC are non-EIIS systems directly involved in the failure chain, not design-context mentions. No BACKED_UP_BY edges — DIDA algorithms (PBA/GRBA/ABA) are described as backup detection methods to CDA but not stated as operable backups to the failed function itself (they are part of the same OPRM trip system, not an independent system backup to the consequence). Previous-occurrence search found no similar events, so no SIMILAR_TO edge/stub LER emitted per rule 9 (nothing to reference)."
